# port/env/dram - Phase-1 behavioral DRAM environment

Copies (never moved) of the Sun behavioral DDR2+ECC channel models:

- `cmp_dram.v`, `ch_mem.v`, `cmp_dram_mon.v`, `dimm_if_mon.v`,
  `dram_mon.v`, `cmp_mem.v`  <- ~/t1_dram_models/env_cmp/
- `cross_module.h` is not copied here; the monitors include the canonical
  `verif/env/cmp/cross_module.h` via `-Iverif/env/cmp` in the Makefile.
- The original Sun `dimm.v` backup was removed; `dimm_mem.v` is the
  Denali-free port of that model.

Icarus-Verilog adaptations (documented inline, marked "IVPORT"):

1. `cmp_dram.v`: all cross-module `force`/`release` statements commented
   out (382, marked IVPORT-NOP); the two always blocks and the
   WARM_RESET initial block that referenced `DCTLPATH*.dram_que.* via
   XMR deleted; the cmp_dram_mon instantiation guarded with
   `IVPORT_NO_MON (defined by `make cmp-build`).
2. `dimm_stub.v`: replacement for dimm.v, which needs the Denali PLI
   tasks $read_mem/$write_mem - unavailable without SJM/PLI.  Stub keeps
   the same port list, tri-states the data pins (inert DIMMs) so ch_mem
   elaborates.  The default build uses the functional `dimm_mem.v`.
3. Not compiled in Phase 1 (iverilog cannot handle their pervasive XMR):
   `cmp_dram_mon.v`, `dram_mon.v`, `cmp_mem.v` (hierarchical task
   assignments, cmp_mem.v:33,367).

Wire-up reference: verif/env/cmp/cmp_top.v:607 (cmp_dram inst),
cmp_top.v:634 (DRAMx_RST_L <- cmp_grst_out_l), cmp_top.v:671 (dram_gclk).
